---
import TrustPage from '../components/TrustPage.astro';
import { soc2Shown, trust } from '../data/trust';

const { type, auditor, period } = trust.soc2;
---

<TrustPage
  title="Security and compliance"
  description="How GeurtsGaming keeps its site and games safe: the way the site is built, and how it follows COPPA."
  heading="Security and compliance"
  lede="The safest information is the information we never have. This site is built to hold as little as possible, and what is left is looked after properly."
>
  <div class="summary">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      {soc2Shown && <li><strong>SOC 2.</strong> An independent auditor has examined how GeurtsGaming looks after security.</li>}
      <li><strong>COPPA.</strong> This site is built to follow the US law that protects children's privacy online.</li>
      <li><strong>Very little to protect.</strong> No accounts, no passwords and no payments on this site.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  {soc2Shown && (
    <Fragment>
      <h2>SOC 2</h2>
      <p>
        SOC 2 is an examination, carried out by an independent auditor, of how a company protects the systems and
        information it is responsible for. GeurtsGaming has completed one{type ? ` (${type})` : ''}. The examination
        was carried out by {auditor}. It covers {period}.
      </p>
      <p>
        Schools, districts and partners can ask for the report at
        <a href={`mailto:${trust.email}`}>{trust.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  )}

  <h2>COPPA</h2>
  <p>
    The Children's Online Privacy Protection Act limits what websites may collect from children under 13. This
    site is built to follow it by not asking children for personal information at all. The
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> lists everything the site does with information.
  </p>

  <h2>How this site is built</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No accounts, passwords or payments.</strong> There is nothing to log in to and nothing to buy here, so there are no passwords or card numbers for anyone to steal.</li>
    <li><strong>Encrypted connections.</strong> Every page is delivered over HTTPS. A request made without it is sent to the secure address.</li>
    <li><strong>Plain pages.</strong> The site is a set of ready-made pages. There is no database behind them.</li>
    <li><strong>A small game server.</strong> The arcade demo's server holds only game information (a random pilot number, a made-up callsign, scores and ship positions) and forgets a pilot about two minutes after they leave.</li>
    <li><strong>No advertising networks.</strong> The pages load their fonts and code from this site. The one outside service is Google Analytics, set up as the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> describes.</li>
    <li><strong>Checked before it goes live.</strong> Every change is checked automatically for mistakes before it is published, and the arcade demo's rules are covered by automated tests.</li>
    <li><strong>Open to inspection.</strong> The site's code is public on <a href="https://github.com/davewgeurts/geurtsgaming" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>, so anyone can see exactly what it does.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Telling us about a problem</h2>
  <p>
    If you find a security problem in this site or in one of our games, please write to
    <a href={`mailto:${trust.email}`}>{trust.email}</a>. Tell us what you found and how to see it, and give us a
    chance to fix it before you tell anyone else. We read every report and will write back.
  </p>
</TrustPage>
